  "development_disclosure": "This v14.14 screen was designed only after the frozen v14.13 preflight finished with no eligible learned checkpoint. v14.13 showed that anchor state replay, PPO-level trust regions, and iterative projection could meet same-batch constraints but did not transfer to unseen deterministic closed-loop trajectories. v14.14 therefore evaluates each joint upper and lower actor update on two independent roots crossed with all four training disturbances. It backtracks or rejects the actor transaction whenever the actual 2% reward floor is violated or the frozen-anchor five-endpoint frequency rank worsens. Critics and duals retain their on-policy update. Guard roots are training constraints and are disjoint from training, checkpoint-selection, and held-out roots. Outer-only and matched v14.13 inner-mechanism controls isolate causality. Only joint outer-guard arms with a nonzero accepted actor update, a trained selected checkpoint, and zero selection and held-out paired violations may authorize expansion. This is development evidence only.",
